    "collapsible_content_fLKhY3": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_yVijMN": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Preparing Your Home for a New Dog",
            "icon": "paw_print",
            "row_content": "<p>Bringing home a new pup is an exciting milestone, but a little preparation goes a long way in ensuring a smooth transition. Start by setting up a comfortable dog bed in a quiet spot, and make sure you have plenty of pet food on hand. Potty training is a key part of those first few weeks, so be ready with a plan and the right supplies. For car rides and future getaways, a sturdy pet carrier and travel accessories are must-haves. Don’t forget to stock up on poop bags and a securely affixed leash for those first walks around the neighborhood. With thoughtful planning, you’ll create a welcoming space where your new furry friend feels right at home.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_ytz9U9": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Grooming Essentials",
            "icon": "paw_print",
            "row_content": "<p>Keeping your dog looking and feeling their best starts with the right grooming essentials. Every dog owner should have a reliable brush, gentle shampoo, and nail clippers suited to their pup’s needs. Regular grooming not only keeps pet hair and dirt under control but also helps prevent physically pains and discomfort. Bath time can be a breeze with tools like the aquapaw pet bathing tool, which makes rinsing and cleaning stress free for both you and your furry friend. Don’t forget to check and trim your dog’s nails regularly—your pet will thank you for the extra comfort and care.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_MhKp4x": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Feeding and Hydration",
            "icon": "paw_print",
            "row_content": "<p>A healthy dog starts with a balanced diet and plenty of fresh water. Choose a high-quality pet food that meets your dog’s unique nutritional needs, and consider using a Yeti’s bowl for mealtime. Consult your veterinarian to ensure you are meeting your dog's dietary requirements. For hydration, a leak proof water bowl that holds up to eight cups is ideal, especially for active pups. Make sure your dog’s food and water bowls are securely affixed and chosen based on your dog's specific needs to prevent spills and keep feeding areas tidy. As a responsible pet owner, keep an eye on your dog’s food intake and adjust portions as needed to support their health and happiness.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_yCHAq6": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Dog Health and Wellness",
            "icon": "paw_print",
            "row_content": "<p>A happy, healthy pup starts with a strong foundation of wellness. As a responsible pet owner, regular checkups with your vet are essential for keeping your dog in top shape. Stay on top of vaccinations, flea and tick prevention, and routine dental care—these small steps can make a big difference in your dog’s long-term health. Accessories like dental chews, calming dog beds, and supportive harnesses can help maintain both physical and mental well-being. Don’t forget to provide plenty of toys for mental stimulation and exercise, which are just as important for your dog’s happiness as nutritious food and a cozy bed. By prioritizing your dog’s health and wellness, you’ll ensure your good boy or girl enjoys every adventure by your side.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_HkLcdw": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Dog Accessories for Specific Needs",
            "icon": "paw_print",
            "row_content": "<p>Every dog is unique, and the best dog accessories are those that cater to your pup’s individual needs. For energetic pit mixes or little chonk breeds, a sturdy harness can make walks safer and more enjoyable. Puppies and new pups benefit from gentle collars and adjustable leashes designed for their smaller size, while senior dogs may appreciate orthopedic beds and easy-step car seats for comfortable travel. If you’re tackling potty training, look for accessories that make the process easier, like absorbent pads and leak proof mats. For those who love outdoor adventures or frequent car rides, a secure car seat or harness keeps your furry friend safe in the back seat. No matter your dog’s age or breed, there’s an accessory out there to make life easier and more fun for both of you.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_EhzHrj": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Choosing the Best Dog Accessories",
            "icon": "paw_print",
            "row_content": "<p>Selecting the right accessories for your dog can feel overwhelming, but a few simple tips can help you make the best choices. Start by measuring your dog to ensure you pick the right size for collars, harnesses, and beds—comfort and safety always come first. Look for durable materials that can withstand daily wear and tear, especially if your pup loves outdoor adventures or has a habit of chewing. Features like a nonslip base on food and water bowls, or a securely affixed leash, can make a world of difference in your daily routine. Consider your lifestyle, too: city dwellers might prefer compact, easy-to-clean accessories, while active owners may need gear that stands up to hiking and travel. With options available in seven sizes, two sizes, and a rainbow of colors, you’re sure to find the best dog accessories to suit every adorable little nugget in your life.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_K9Hdh4": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Traveling with Your Dog",
            "icon": "paw_print",
            "row_content": "<p>Traveling with your dog can be a fun and stress free experience with the right accessories. A comfortable pet carrier or car seat keeps your furry friend safe and secure during car rides, whether you’re heading out for errands or planning a road trip. Using a dog car seat cover helps protect your vehicle from dirt, hair, and moisture, while accessories like harnesses or seat belts protect your dog during travel. Remember to pack essentials like food, water, and poop bags, and bring along a portable water bowl for hydration on the go. Favorite toys and treats can help keep your dog entertained and relaxed during longer journeys. With a bit of planning and the best travel accessories, every trip becomes an adventure you and your dog will love.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_hEHGWm": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Tips for New Puppy Owners",
            "icon": "paw_print",
            "row_content": "<p>Whether you’re a seasoned dog owner or welcoming a new puppy into your home, a few smart strategies can make life with your furry friend even more enjoyable. Keep pet hair under control with regular brushing and invest in accessories that make bath time a breeze—tools like the aquapaw pet bathing tool can divert water exactly where you need it, making cleanup quick and stress free. If your dog gives you the stink eye after a muddy walk, a garden hose with an included adapter can help wash away dirt before it gets inside. Living in City apartments or other tight spaces? Choose compact beds and storage-friendly accessories to maximize your space. For road trips and car rides, always have a stash of poop bags, a portable water bowl, and a comfy car seat ready to go. And don’t forget to trade tips with other pet owners—sometimes the best advice comes from those who’ve walked in your shoes (or with your pup at their loyal heel). With the right approach and a few clever accessories, every day with your dog can be a new adventure.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
